What this project is not
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DLSS, DLSS 5, Neural Rendering, NGX and nvngx_dlssnr.dll are NVIDIA Corporation's.
This project is an independent reimplementation of the inference pass so that it can
run on an Intel Xe2 GPU. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by
NVIDIA, and no NVIDIA source code is included.

**No model weights and no NVIDIA binary are distributed here, and none ever will be.**
The repository is source text only. To run anything you must supply your own copy of
`nvngx_dlssnr.dll` and extract the weights from it yourself; the README says how.
Whether you are entitled to that copy is between you and whoever gave it to you.

`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and the notes under `notes/` describe what was measured about that
binary — the recovered graph, tensor shapes, and the names of kernels demangled from its
embedded code. They are published deliberately, as a record of analysis rather than a copy
of the thing analysed: no NVIDIA code, no weights and no verbatim transcription of their
material is included, and what is here is regenerable by anyone holding the same file.

Comparison images live on the `media` branch, not in the code history. They are frames
from commercial games — Tekken 7 © Bandai Namco Entertainment, Dead or Alive 5 Last Round
© Koei Tecmo Games, Mortal Kombat 1 © Warner Bros. Entertainment Inc. and its guest
characters' respective owners — shown to compare a rendering
technique, and they remain their publishers' property.

